NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You know you need a generic interrupt. You do not know which phase to pause\nin. If you pause too early, the model has no draft to review. If you pause too\nlate, a tool has already run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By the end of this page you can pick one phase from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"INTERRUPT_BOUNDARY_PHASES"},{"type":"text","value":" and write the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.phase"},{"type":"text","value":" guard for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the define, register, and resolve steps, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generic Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-four-phases","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The four phases"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" runs at each of these points in one agent iteration.\nReturn "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ interrupts }"},{"type":"text","value":" to pause. Return nothing to let the run continue."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Phase"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When it runs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typical question"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" for this iteration, before the adapter call"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do we have enough from the user to spend tokens?"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterModel"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After the model stream ends, before tools run"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Is this draft or these tool calls acceptable?"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After the assistant tool-call message is in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", before execution"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"May these tools run?"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After tools finish and their result messages are in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"May these results go back to the model?"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine combines every request from every middleware at the same phase into\none interrupt batch. That batch ends the current run with one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupt"},{"type":"text","value":"\noutcome."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const requestReview: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'request-review',\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    if (ctx.iteration !== 0) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'initial-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n          payload: {\n            title: 'Release plan',\n            changes: ['Add search', 'Add tests'],\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot change config. It can only pause. To change\nprompts, tools, or messages from the user answer, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./apply-answers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Apply Answers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"skip-the-pause-on-the-continuation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skip the pause on the continuation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The continuation is a new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. Every boundary hook runs again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you return the same request, the run pauses again. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" is\nset, skip the emit. Use that skip when the pause belongs to the original\nrequest only."}]},{"type":"code","value":"onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n  if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n  if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n  return {\n    interrupts: [\n      reviewPlan.interrupt({\n        key: 'initial-plan',\n        reason: 'review-required',\n        message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n        payload: {\n          title: 'Release plan',\n          changes: ['Add search'],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  }\n}","lang":"ts","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-you-can-read-at-each-phase","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you can read at each phase"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every hook receives the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddlewareContext"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"contents"}]},{"type":"text","value":" change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Useful fields on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"phase"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"iteration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parentRunId"},{"type":"text","value":" (set on a continuation)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" (read-only view)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolNames"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasTools"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accumulatedContent"},{"type":"text","value":" (assistant text for this model turn)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"},{"type":"text","value":" (fixed for this request)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" (your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ context })"},{"type":"text","value":" value)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abort(reason)"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defer(promise)"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutating "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.messages"},{"type":"text","value":" does not change the engine config."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"beforemodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" for this iteration has already run. Prompts, tools, messages, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" are the values after that merge."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accumulatedContent"},{"type":"text","value":" is empty"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" is the conversation so far"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this phase when you need data "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"before"}]},{"type":"text","value":" you pay for a model call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aftermodel","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterModel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model stream is complete."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"accumulatedContent"},{"type":"text","value":" has this turn's assistant text"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" does "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" include this turn yet"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Proposed tool calls are not on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx"},{"type":"text","value":". They are not in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" yet"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need tool names or args, wait for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"},{"type":"text","value":", or watch "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"\nduring "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelStream"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"beforetools","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The engine has added the assistant message with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCalls"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":".\nTools have not run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this phase to inspect the proposed calls before any side effect."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aftertools","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools have run. Result messages with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"role: 'tool'"},{"type":"text","value":" are already in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onToolPhaseComplete"},{"type":"text","value":" has already run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this phase to inspect results before the next model turn."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"real-uses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Real uses"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"beforemodel-collect-a-choice-first","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":": collect a choice first"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ask for a plan, an audience, or a locale before the model writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Which brand voice should this reply use?\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Which ticket should I work on?\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"Is this request in scope for this agent?\""}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aftermodel-review-the-draft","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterModel"},{"type":"text","value":": review the draft"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model has written text. You want a human to accept it before tools run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review an email draft before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendEmail"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review a SQL query before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runQuery"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review a support reply before it reaches the user"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"beforetools-gate-the-side-effects","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeTools"},{"type":"text","value":": gate the side effects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model asked for tools. Nothing has executed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confirm a bulk delete"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confirm a payment"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Confirm a deploy"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is close to "},{"type":"link","href":"./tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool approval"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use a generic interrupt\nwhen the question is not a yes or no on one tool. Also use it when several\ntools must be judged as one batch."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"aftertools-audit-the-results","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterTools"},{"type":"text","value":": audit the results"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tools have already run. You want a human to see the output before the\nmodel uses it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A search returned customer PII. Ask if it may stay in context"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A code run produced a diff. Ask if the next turn may apply it"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A lookup returned a low-confidence match. Ask which record to keep"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"try-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Try it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React chat example has a playground for all four phases."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-chat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/generic-interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick a phase and resolve both cards."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you are ready to apply the answer to prompts or to stop the run, go to\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./apply-answers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Apply Answers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-four-phases","text":"The four phases","level":2},{"id":"skip-the-pause-on-the-continuation","text":"Skip the pause on the continuation","level":2},{"id":"what-you-can-read-at-each-phase","text":"What you can read at each phase","level":2},{"id":"beforemodel","text":"beforeModel","level":3},{"id":"aftermodel","text":"afterModel","level":3},{"id":"beforetools","text":"beforeTools","level":3},{"id":"aftertools","text":"afterTools","level":3},{"id":"real-uses","text":"Real uses","level":2},{"id":"beforemodel-collect-a-choice-first","text":"beforeModel: collect a choice first","level":3},{"id":"aftermodel-review-the-draft","text":"afterModel: review the draft","level":3},{"id":"beforetools-gate-the-side-effects","text":"beforeTools: gate the side effects","level":3},{"id":"aftertools-audit-the-results","text":"afterTools: audit the results","level":3},{"id":"try-it","text":"Try it","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou know you need a generic interrupt. You do not know which phase to pause\nin. If you pause too early, the model has no draft to review. If you pause too\nlate, a tool has already run.\n\nBy the end of this page you can pick one phase from\n`INTERRUPT_BOUNDARY_PHASES` and write the `ctx.phase` guard for it.\n\nFor the define, register, and resolve steps, see\n[Generic Interrupts](./generic).\n\n## The four phases\n\n`onInterruptBoundary` runs at each of these points in one agent iteration.\nReturn `{ interrupts }` to pause. Return nothing to let the run continue.\n\n| Phase | When it runs | Typical question |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `beforeModel` | After `onConfig` for this iteration, before the adapter call | Do we have enough from the user to spend tokens? |\n| `afterModel` | After the model stream ends, before tools run | Is this draft or these tool calls acceptable? |\n| `beforeTools` | After the assistant tool-call message is in `messages`, before execution | May these tools run? |\n| `afterTools` | After tools finish and their result messages are in `messages` | May these results go back to the model? |\n\nThe engine combines every request from every middleware at the same phase into\none interrupt batch. That batch ends the current run with one `interrupt`\noutcome.\n\n```ts\nimport type { ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const requestReview: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'request-review',\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    if (ctx.iteration !== 0) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'initial-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n          payload: {\n            title: 'Release plan',\n            changes: ['Add search', 'Add tests'],\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\n`onInterruptBoundary` cannot change config. It can only pause. To change\nprompts, tools, or messages from the user answer, see\n[Apply Answers](./apply-answers).\n\n## Skip the pause on the continuation\n\nThe continuation is a new `chat()` call. Every boundary hook runs again.\n\nIf you return the same request, the run pauses again. If `ctx.parentRunId` is\nset, skip the emit. Use that skip when the pause belongs to the original\nrequest only.\n\n```ts ignore\nonInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n  if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n  if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n  return {\n    interrupts: [\n      reviewPlan.interrupt({\n        key: 'initial-plan',\n        reason: 'review-required',\n        message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n        payload: {\n          title: 'Release plan',\n          changes: ['Add search'],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## What you can read at each phase\n\nEvery hook receives the same `ChatMiddlewareContext`. The **contents** change.\n\nUseful fields on `ctx`:\n\n- `phase` and `iteration`\n- `parentRunId` (set on a continuation)\n- `messages` (read-only view)\n- `systemPrompts`, `toolNames`, `hasTools`, `modelOptions`\n- `accumulatedContent` (assistant text for this model turn)\n- `model` and `provider` (fixed for this request)\n- `context` (your `chat({ context })` value)\n- `abort(reason)` and `defer(promise)`\n\nMutating `ctx.messages` does not change the engine config.\n\n### `beforeModel`\n\n`onConfig` for this iteration has already run. Prompts, tools, messages, and\n`modelOptions` are the values after that merge.\n\n- `accumulatedContent` is empty\n- `messages` is the conversation so far\n\nUse this phase when you need data **before** you pay for a model call.\n\n### `afterModel`\n\nThe model stream is complete.\n\n- `accumulatedContent` has this turn's assistant text\n- `messages` does **not** include this turn yet\n- Proposed tool calls are not on `ctx`. They are not in `messages` yet\n\nIf you need tool names or args, wait for `beforeTools`, or watch `onChunk`\nduring `modelStream`.\n\n### `beforeTools`\n\nThe engine has added the assistant message with `toolCalls` to `messages`.\nTools have not run.\n\nUse this phase to inspect the proposed calls before any side effect.\n\n### `afterTools`\n\nTools have run. Result messages with `role: 'tool'` are already in\n`messages`. `onToolPhaseComplete` has already run.\n\nUse this phase to inspect results before the next model turn.\n\n## Real uses\n\n### `beforeModel`: collect a choice first\n\nAsk for a plan, an audience, or a locale before the model writes.\n\nExamples:\n\n- \"Which brand voice should this reply use?\"\n- \"Which ticket should I work on?\"\n- \"Is this request in scope for this agent?\"\n\n### `afterModel`: review the draft\n\nThe model has written text. You want a human to accept it before tools run.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Review an email draft before `sendEmail`\n- Review a SQL query before `runQuery`\n- Review a support reply before it reaches the user\n\n### `beforeTools`: gate the side effects\n\nThe model asked for tools. Nothing has executed.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Confirm a bulk delete\n- Confirm a payment\n- Confirm a deploy\n\nThis is close to [tool approval](./tool-approval). Use a generic interrupt\nwhen the question is not a yes or no on one tool. Also use it when several\ntools must be judged as one batch.\n\n### `afterTools`: audit the results\n\nThe tools have already run. You want a human to see the output before the\nmodel uses it.\n\nExamples:\n\n- A search returned customer PII. Ask if it may stay in context\n- A code run produced a diff. Ask if the next turn may apply it\n- A lookup returned a low-confidence match. Ask which record to keep\n\n## Try it\n\nThe React chat example has a playground for all four phases.\n\n1. Start `examples/ts-react-chat`.\n2. Open `/generic-interrupts`.\n3. Pick a phase and resolve both cards.\n\nWhen you are ready to apply the answer to prompts or to stop the run, go to\n[Apply Answers](./apply-answers).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Lifecycle Boundaries\nid: interrupts-boundaries\norder: 5\ndescription: \"Pick the chat lifecycle phase where a generic interrupt pauses the run.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - generic interrupt\n  - onInterruptBoundary\n  - INTERRUPT_BOUNDARY_PHASES\n  - beforeModel\n  - afterModel\n  - beforeTools\n  - afterTools\n---\n\nYou know you need a generic interrupt. You do not know which phase to pause\nin. If you pause too early, the model has no draft to review. If you pause too\nlate, a tool has already run.\n\nBy the end of this page you can pick one phase from\n`INTERRUPT_BOUNDARY_PHASES` and write the `ctx.phase` guard for it.\n\nFor the define, register, and resolve steps, see\n[Generic Interrupts](./generic).\n\n## The four phases\n\n`onInterruptBoundary` runs at each of these points in one agent iteration.\nReturn `{ interrupts }` to pause. Return nothing to let the run continue.\n\n| Phase | When it runs | Typical question |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `beforeModel` | After `onConfig` for this iteration, before the adapter call | Do we have enough from the user to spend tokens? |\n| `afterModel` | After the model stream ends, before tools run | Is this draft or these tool calls acceptable? |\n| `beforeTools` | After the assistant tool-call message is in `messages`, before execution | May these tools run? |\n| `afterTools` | After tools finish and their result messages are in `messages` | May these results go back to the model? |\n\nThe engine combines every request from every middleware at the same phase into\none interrupt batch. That batch ends the current run with one `interrupt`\noutcome.\n\n```ts\nimport type { ChatMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reviewPlan } from './interrupts'\n\nexport const requestReview: ChatMiddleware<unknown, typeof reviewPlan> = {\n  name: 'request-review',\n  onInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n    if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n    if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n    if (ctx.iteration !== 0) return\n    return {\n      interrupts: [\n        reviewPlan.interrupt({\n          key: 'initial-plan',\n          reason: 'review-required',\n          message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n          payload: {\n            title: 'Release plan',\n            changes: ['Add search', 'Add tests'],\n          },\n        }),\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n}\n```\n\n`onInterruptBoundary` cannot change config. It can only pause. To change\nprompts, tools, or messages from the user answer, see\n[Apply Answers](./apply-answers).\n\n## Skip the pause on the continuation\n\nThe continuation is a new `chat()` call. Every boundary hook runs again.\n\nIf you return the same request, the run pauses again. If `ctx.parentRunId` is\nset, skip the emit. Use that skip when the pause belongs to the original\nrequest only.\n\n```ts ignore\nonInterruptBoundary(ctx) {\n  if (ctx.phase !== 'beforeModel') return\n  if (ctx.parentRunId) return\n  return {\n    interrupts: [\n      reviewPlan.interrupt({\n        key: 'initial-plan',\n        reason: 'review-required',\n        message: 'Review the proposed plan.',\n        payload: {\n          title: 'Release plan',\n          changes: ['Add search'],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## What you can read at each phase\n\nEvery hook receives the same `ChatMiddlewareContext`. The **contents** change.\n\nUseful fields on `ctx`:\n\n- `phase` and `iteration`\n- `parentRunId` (set on a continuation)\n- `messages` (read-only view)\n- `systemPrompts`, `toolNames`, `hasTools`, `modelOptions`\n- `accumulatedContent` (assistant text for this model turn)\n- `model` and `provider` (fixed for this request)\n- `context` (your `chat({ context })` value)\n- `abort(reason)` and `defer(promise)`\n\nMutating `ctx.messages` does not change the engine config.\n\n### `beforeModel`\n\n`onConfig` for this iteration has already run. Prompts, tools, messages, and\n`modelOptions` are the values after that merge.\n\n- `accumulatedContent` is empty\n- `messages` is the conversation so far\n\nUse this phase when you need data **before** you pay for a model call.\n\n### `afterModel`\n\nThe model stream is complete.\n\n- `accumulatedContent` has this turn's assistant text\n- `messages` does **not** include this turn yet\n- Proposed tool calls are not on `ctx`. They are not in `messages` yet\n\nIf you need tool names or args, wait for `beforeTools`, or watch `onChunk`\nduring `modelStream`.\n\n### `beforeTools`\n\nThe engine has added the assistant message with `toolCalls` to `messages`.\nTools have not run.\n\nUse this phase to inspect the proposed calls before any side effect.\n\n### `afterTools`\n\nTools have run. Result messages with `role: 'tool'` are already in\n`messages`. `onToolPhaseComplete` has already run.\n\nUse this phase to inspect results before the next model turn.\n\n## Real uses\n\n### `beforeModel`: collect a choice first\n\nAsk for a plan, an audience, or a locale before the model writes.\n\nExamples:\n\n- \"Which brand voice should this reply use?\"\n- \"Which ticket should I work on?\"\n- \"Is this request in scope for this agent?\"\n\n### `afterModel`: review the draft\n\nThe model has written text. You want a human to accept it before tools run.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Review an email draft before `sendEmail`\n- Review a SQL query before `runQuery`\n- Review a support reply before it reaches the user\n\n### `beforeTools`: gate the side effects\n\nThe model asked for tools. Nothing has executed.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Confirm a bulk delete\n- Confirm a payment\n- Confirm a deploy\n\nThis is close to [tool approval](./tool-approval). Use a generic interrupt\nwhen the question is not a yes or no on one tool. Also use it when several\ntools must be judged as one batch.\n\n### `afterTools`: audit the results\n\nThe tools have already run. You want a human to see the output before the\nmodel uses it.\n\nExamples:\n\n- A search returned customer PII. Ask if it may stay in context\n- A code run produced a diff. Ask if the next turn may apply it\n- A lookup returned a low-confidence match. Ask which record to keep\n\n## Try it\n\nThe React chat example has a playground for all four phases.\n\n1. Start `examples/ts-react-chat`.\n2. Open `/generic-interrupts`.\n3. Pick a phase and resolve both cards.\n\nWhen you are ready to apply the answer to prompts or to stop the run, go to\n[Apply Answers](./apply-answers).\n"}
